WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.088
 ♪  

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:08.883
 For me, I got to get my poop, 
 so to speak, in a square. 

00:00:08.925 --> 00:00:12.804
 Tighten it up so that I'm 
 super Sue again. 

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:14.514
 But how do I do that? 

00:00:14.556 --> 00:00:17.350
 These are the two 
 overflow tents, 

00:00:17.392 --> 00:00:20.395
 and I'm not gonna have people 
 using them for quite a while. 

00:00:20.437 --> 00:00:23.023
 So I want to annex this one 

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:29.446
 and make it into my physical 
 improvement center, the gym. 

00:00:29.487 --> 00:00:32.407
 I don't have a big weight set 
 and a barbell 

00:00:32.449 --> 00:00:35.368
 and you know, urgh, 
 things to lay down on. 

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:38.079
 And that's, that's not 
 the kind of improvement, 

00:00:38.121 --> 00:00:40.373
 physical improvement, 
 I'm looking for. 

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:43.418
 What I'm trying to do is, 
 as I age, 

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.045
 the arthritis is setting in. 

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:47.464
 The range of motion 
 is decreasing. 

00:00:47.505 --> 00:00:51.217
 The bears stay just as damn fast 
 as the moment they were born. 

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:57.432
 And I can't compete unless I 
 improve slightly where I'm at. 

00:00:57.474 --> 00:01:00.310
 ♪  

00:01:00.351 --> 00:01:04.314
 I'm not looking to be 
 Susie Schwarzenegger. 

00:01:04.355 --> 00:01:06.357
 I'm not the Sue-minator. 

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:09.819
 I'm flexi-Sue. 

00:01:09.861 --> 00:01:13.865
 What I'm looking for is weight, 
 not heavy weight. 

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:17.410
 Light weights to work 
 my range of motion. 

00:01:19.204 --> 00:01:21.831
 A cone on the runway 
 got in my way, 

00:01:21.873 --> 00:01:23.625
 and I went down 
 like a little infant 

00:01:23.666 --> 00:01:25.585
 not getting the candy bar. 

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:30.423
 I can't have fracturing going on 
 and instability 

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:33.843
 and expect to have 
 a top-notch-running place. 

00:01:33.885 --> 00:01:38.431
 So I got some rope here, 
 got some pulleys here. 

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.683
 My body is hurting. 

00:01:40.725 --> 00:01:45.563
 The pain that this shoulder, 
 whatever, is putting me through, 

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:51.402
 it's one more thing 
 in this cacophony of things 

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:54.948
 that's just riotously 
 making me break down. 

00:01:54.989 --> 00:01:58.243
 I've got to do 
 my own form of therapy. 

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:02.747
 ♪  

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:05.792
 ♪  

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:09.337
 It's time to get myself together 

00:02:09.379 --> 00:02:13.299
 and, uh, maybe see 
 what I want to construct. 

00:02:13.341 --> 00:02:17.303
 I'm approaching 60, 
 at 60 miles an hour. 

00:02:17.345 --> 00:02:21.141
 I don't have angst 
 about getting older, per se, 

00:02:21.182 --> 00:02:25.562
 but I can tell you, a body, 
 it's not regenerating anymore. 

00:02:25.603 --> 00:02:27.480
 You're on the downhill cycle. 

00:02:27.522 --> 00:02:31.401
 We are all gonna have 
 that epiphany that says 

00:02:31.442 --> 00:02:36.823
 you now officially have lived 

00:02:36.865 --> 00:02:39.367
 more years than you 
 are going to live. 

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.914
 Maybe everybody else's 
 road to health 

00:02:44.956 --> 00:02:46.833
 is, is paved 
 with good intentions 

00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:48.793
 and, and the golden staircase. 

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:53.464
 Mine: rust, grease, 
 a little ingenuity. 

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:56.301
 This is just a piece of, 
 pieces of junk. 

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:57.802
 An old rim. 

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.721
 Old electrical stuff. 

00:02:59.762 --> 00:03:01.472
 But really simple. 

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:06.060
 You're just forcing your body 

00:03:06.102 --> 00:03:09.189
 to lay open and stretch. 

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:11.566
 All of this is stretching out. 

00:03:11.608 --> 00:03:16.946
 The other interesting thing 
 that I can do, 

00:03:16.988 --> 00:03:19.032
 grab it and come up with it. 

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.535
 Grab it and come up with it. 

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:25.622
 (clanging) 

00:03:25.663 --> 00:03:28.917
 I wanted to add weight. 

00:03:28.958 --> 00:03:30.627
 Now... 

00:03:30.668 --> 00:03:33.504
 there's a lot you can do, 

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:39.886
 and I didn't pay this 
 incredible price to get it done. 

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:42.555
 The Sue gym is operational. 

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:43.973
 This isn't gonna fix everything. 

00:03:44.015 --> 00:03:45.266
 This is one part. 

00:03:45.308 --> 00:03:47.352
 The mind, the body, the spirit. 

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:51.731
 But it's gonna take me from 
 waiting for the next problem 

00:03:51.773 --> 00:03:54.484
 to hell yeah, 
 I found a solution. 

00:03:54.525 --> 00:03:55.777
 ♪  

